.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt BSD3-VT-GUARD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bsd3-vt-guard
.Nd supervise a bounded desktop trial and restore console state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar seconds evidence-directory
.Fl -
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This root-only program is never setuid.
It refuses an existing process-controlled VT and snapshots available consoles,
including VT mode, keyboard/display modes, terminal settings and ownership.
The command runs under a separate timeout controller.
The parent remains a native process reaper with a longer deadline and confines
termination to its own descendants.
Afterward it reopens the consoles, restores their saved state and checks readback,
including the original active VT.
It does not change power policy, networking, boot selection or rc.conf.
.Pp
The deadline is between1 and600 seconds.
A new private evidence directory is required.
The readiness files identify the separate guard/controller processes;
verify them while workload output is still streaming.
The command-exit file precedes final recovery evidence.
Only complete.txt is the final evidence barrier.
A timeout, signal request, forced termination or failed restore is recorded as
failure or assisted recovery, never as an unassisted pass.
The parent allows fifteen seconds beyond the inner deadline, followed by bounded
termination and restoration waits.
.Pp
KVM is allowed by default.
Physical hardware additionally requires
.Ev BSD3_ALLOW_HARDWARE_TRIAL=yes
and an explicitly coordinated operator window with a preserved boot fallback.
This flag is not permission to interrupt someone else's experiment.
A kernel freeze or SIGKILL of the guard cannot be repaired by this process.
No GPU presentation guarantee follows from restored terminal settings.
.Pp
Use immutable, reviewed root-owned copies of any trial scripts and preserve their
hashes with matching source/package identities.
Run detached from SSH with a separate control connection.
Never install this program with elevated mode bits or grant unrestricted sudo
as part of a test.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Zero means the command exited zero without intervention and console restoration
passed.
Nonzero includes timeout, interruption, descendant cleanup intervention,
command failure or incomplete recovery.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bsd3-session 1 ,
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr procctl 2 ,
.Xr timeout 1
